From: kristofferR <481270+kristofferR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ao_spatial: render TrueHD Atmos and DTS:X with SpatialAudioBridge

The output owns SpatialAudioBridge's passthrough sink, its synchronizer and
the clock. SpatialAudioBridge is compiled from pinned sources by mpv-build.
There is no application callback, raw-address option or installed
spatial-audio header. The clock runs only over audio the renderer holds,
from the sink's progress and queue. A refused stream latches its format and
reopens for mpv's PCM decode path. Volume changes and end-of-stream reach the
sink through private functions.

